{
	"id": "reduckHackerNews",
	"name": "Top Hacker News stories, on a webhook (Reduck)",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Top Hacker News stories, on a webhook\n\nCall `GET /webhook/hacker-news` and get the 10 top stories of the Hacker News front page as JSON: rank, title, url, points and comments.\n\nThe Reduck node runs the script `reduck/news.ycombinator.com/top_stories` on a Reduck managed browser that connects from a US home address (**Country**: US): Hacker News refuses many requests from a datacenter. The site needs no sign-in, so you install nothing.\n\nThe Reduck node uses the credential `reduckQuickStart`: the README's quick start makes it from your API key.",
				"height": 300,
				"width": 420
			},
			"id": "4d0f3a8e-6a51-4c1b-9d0e-2a7c1f5b8e01",
			"name": "About",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [-460, -140]
		},
		{
